      "writtenOn": "2017-02-01T12:23:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For tcpci_tcpm_drv, I would implement the get_fw_version() the following way:\nit dumps and records the mandatory registers VENDOR_ID/PRODUCT_ID/DEVICE_ID\n(actually USBTYPEC_REV/USBPD_REV_VER/PD_INTERFACE_REV looks useful , maybe you should have them to the message)\nthen it has a switch/case statement for the vendor firmware version, e.g:\nswitch(vendor_id) {\n#ifdef CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPM_PS8751\ncase PARADE_VENDOR_ID:\n    fw_version \u003d ps8751_get_fw_version();\n#endif\ndefault:\n    fw_version \u003d -1; /* unknown */\n}\n\nand ps8751_get_fw_version() in driver/tcpm/ps8751.c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 231,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 231,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "0b903502510e665e2b0ed0c4b359d62678750a0f",
